Z||000000||KRMFiero||07-28-2001||05:23 PM||||Okay i took the power antenna out of my Cadilliac before it goes to the junk yard... where could i mount it? is there enough room anywhere on the back clip or something? i know it will not fit on front fenders...<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 Project<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>       <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> <BR>AOL: Physcokyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||07-28-2001||06:08 PM||||I don't know about the Cadillac unit but I have fitted an aftermarket one under the front fender of my car.  It is mounted so that the antenna comes up about 2" behind where the factory unit was.  I moved it back that way so that the power unit clears the inner fender liner.  I filled in the hole in the fender and cut a new one.  The problem is that the unit mounts down so low that the top of the lowered antenna is about 1-2" below the fender.  I have mounted one of the plastic grommet/bezels from the antenna kit onto the fender for the antenna to come up thru. <P>The only thing I don't like is that the antenna is chrome.  The company does have replacement masts and you can get them in black which I may do one day.  Instead of controlling the antenna from the radio, I am going to mount a switch so that I can keep it down when I have the radio on but am just using it to play CDs thru.  <P>Sorry I have no photos at this time.  I will try to get some film for the camera and take a couple of how it is mounted before I bolt the fender back on for good (I hope!)||||reg||1
